OEM vs ODM Furniture: What's the Difference for Buyers?

When sourcing custom furniture from China, buyers often encounter two terms: OEM and ODM.

They sound similar, but they describe different approaches.

OEM Furniture

OEM is generally used when the buyer provides the design or specifications and the manufacturer produces the furniture according to those requirements.

This is useful when a brand already has its own product design.

ODM Furniture

ODM allows the manufacturer to provide existing designs or product-development support that the buyer can customize.

This can be useful for retailers or brands that want to develop products without designing everything from scratch.

Which One Is Better?

It depends on the project.

Have your own drawings? → OEM may fit better.

Need help developing a product? → ODM may be more convenient.

The important thing is to clarify exactly what the factory will provide during the design and sampling stage.

